{
   "description": "Every gateway service: answering now, availability over 24 hours, 7 and 30 days against the 99.5% SLO, error budget, downtime, response time and certificate, and the hosts behind them. Managed by anvil: change dashboards/sla.jsonnet.",
   "editable": false,
   "panels": [
      {
         "datasource": {
            "type": "datasource",
            "uid": "-- Mixed --"
         },
         "gridPos": {
            "h": 4,
            "w": 24,
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0
         },
         "id": 1,
         "options": {
            "content": "Each service is checked every 30 seconds where it runs (its own address and port), or **through the gateway** when it has none of its own (Pi-hole's web page, Homepage, the docs) or sits in the secrets enclave (Vault, Vaultwarden). **Up** means it answers, whatever the page says: a sign-in page or an error below 500 still counts. The **SLO is 99.5%** over 30 days, about **3.6 hours** of downtime allowed: the **error budget** is how much of that is left. The history starts when the checks did, so early on the 30-day figures cover less than 30 days.\n",
            "mode": "markdown"
         },
         "pluginVersion": "v13.0.0",
         "title": "How to read this",
         "type": "text"
      },
